# 中频词汇 List06
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 中频词汇List06核心词汇

{{emission}}{/ɪˈmɪʃn/}{排放；散发}{The country pledged to cut carbon emissions by 40%.}}
{{emotion}}{/ɪˈməʊʃn/}{情感；情绪}{The speech was filled with emotion and sincerity.}}
{{empire}}{/ˈempaɪər/}{帝国；大企业}{The tech empire grew from a small garage startup.}}
{{enterprise}}{/ˈentəpraɪz/}{企业；事业}{Social enterprises combine profit with purpose.}}
{{enthusiasm}}{/ɪnˈθjuːziæzəm/}{热情；热心}{The team's enthusiasm was evident in their presentation.}}
{{entire}}{/ɪnˈtaɪər/}{整个的；全部的}{The entire project was completed ahead of schedule.}}
{{entity}}{/ˈentəti/}{实体；存在}{Each subsidiary operates as a separate legal entity.}}
{{environment}}{/ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt/}{环境；自然环境}{A supportive learning environment boosts student achievement.}}
{{episode}}{/ˈepɪsəʊd/}{插曲；一集}{The documentary covers every episode of the crisis.}}
{{equivalent}}{/ɪˈkwɪvələnt/}{等价的；相当的}{The diploma is equivalent to a bachelor's degree.}}
{{era}}{/ˈɪərə/}{时代；纪元}{We are entering a new era of artificial intelligence.}}
{{essential}}{/ɪˈsenʃl/}{必要的；本质的}{Teamwork is essential for the success of any project.}}
{{ethic}}{/ˈeθɪk/}{道德规范；伦理}{The company operates under a strict code of ethics.}}
{{ethnic}}{/ˈeθnɪk/}{民族的；种族的}{Ethnic diversity enriches the cultural fabric of a nation.}}
{{evident}}{/ˈevɪdənt/}{明显的；显然的}{The benefits of the program are already evident.}}
{{exaggerate}}{/ɪɡˈzædʒəreɪt/}{夸张；夸大}{The report did not exaggerate the severity of the problem.}}
{{examine}}{/ɪɡˈzæmɪn/}{检查；审查}{The court examined the evidence carefully.}}
{{excessive}}{/ɪkˈsesɪv/}{过度的；过多的}{Excessive regulation can stifle innovation.}}
{{exchange}}{/ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ/}{交换；交易所}{The cultural exchange program promotes mutual understanding.}}
{{exclusive}}{/ɪkˈskluːsɪv/}{排他的；独家的}{The hotel offers exclusive access to a private beach.}}
{{exert}}{/ɪɡˈzɜːt/}{施加；发挥}{Parents exert considerable influence on their children's choices.}}
{{exhaust}}{/ɪɡˈzɔːst/}{耗尽；排气}{The marathon exhausted even the most experienced runners.}}
{{exotic}}{/ɪɡˈzɒtɪk/}{异国的；奇异的}{The island is famous for its exotic wildlife.}}
{{expansion}}{/ɪkˈspænʃn/}{扩张；扩展}{The rapid expansion of the company created new job opportunities.}}
{{expertise}}{/ˌekspɜːˈtiːz/}{专业知识；专长}{We need someone with expertise in data science.}}
{{exploitation}}{/ˌeksplɔɪˈteɪʃn/}{开发；剥削}{The exploitation of workers in sweatshops must end.}}
{{explosion}}{/ɪkˈspləʊʒn/}{爆炸；激增}{There has been an explosion of interest in renewable energy.}}
{{exposure}}{/ɪkˈspəʊʒər/}{暴露；曝光}{Exposure to pollution can cause respiratory problems.}}
{{extension}}{/ɪkˈstenʃn/}{延伸；延期}{The deadline extension gave students more time to prepare.}}
{{extent}}{/ɪkˈstent/}{程度；范围}{The full extent of the damage is still being assessed.}}
